// stage1-only
// expect-compile-error x86
// expect-exit: 22
// A str parameter that would overflow the register budget is rejected: v1
// only spills one-word parameters, never a two-word str/struct. arm64's
// M10 stack spill covers it, so on that target the call runs (exit 22).
fn f(a int, b int, c int, d int, e int, f int, g str) int {
	return a + b + c + d + e + f + g.len;
}
fn main() int {
	return f(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, "x");
}
